   "turn": 10,
   "response_text": "Now let me look more closely at the configuration to identify the issue. The sudden degradation at epoch 17 is suspicious. Let me check if there's anything in the config that might cause this:\n\nLooking at the config again:\n- Learning rate: 0.2 (this is VERY high for Adam optimizer with a typical base rate)\n- Batch size: 256\n- Optimizer: adam\n- Epochs: 20\n- No learning rate schedule\n\nThe learning rate of 0.2 is extremely aggressive for Adam. The typical default learning rate for Adam is 0.001, and 0.2 is 200x higher! This would cause:\n1. Unstable training\n2. Erratic loss values\n3. Potential divergence\n\nLooking at the metrics pattern:\n- Epochs 0-16: Training loss stabilizes around 0.38-0.44 with validation accuracy around 0.81-0.85 (convergence)\n- Epochs 17-19: Training loss jumps to 0.53-0.57, validation accuracy drops to 0.75-0.76 (divergence)\n\nThis pattern suggests the model was on a reasonable trajectory, but the high learning rate caused instability that manifested around epoch 17. The loss trend appears to show increasing instability.\n\nLet me double-check the configuration file:",
