   "turn": 11,
   "response_text": "This is confirmed. A learning rate of 0.2 for Adam is unreasonably high and represents a clear misconfiguration. The typical range for Adam is 0.0001 to 0.001. \n\nLet me verify this is the root cause by examining the metric pattern more closely. The degradation starting exactly at epoch 17 with the sudden jump in loss and drop in accuracy is characteristic of a learning rate that's too high - the model hasn't diverged yet but the oscillations are getting worse over time.\n\nBased on my investigation, I've identified an incident:\n\n**Diagnosis:**\n- **Detected:** TRUE\n- **Operator Class:** excessive_learning_rate\n- **Root Cause:** The learning rate is set to 0.2, which is approximately 200-2000x higher than reasonable values for Adam optimizer (typical range: 0.0001-0.001). This causes training instability that manifests as a sudden loss spike and validation accuracy drop starting at epoch 17.\n\n**Evidence:**\n1. Config shows `training.lr = 0.2` (unreasonably high for Adam)\n2. Training loss jumps from ~0.39 (epoch 16) to 0.53 (epoch 17) to 0.57 (epoch 18-19)\n3. Validation accuracy drops from 0.834 (epoch 16) to 0.759 (epoch 17) to 0.753 (epochs 18-19)\n4. The logs show the training completed but with degraded final performance (val_acc=0.7531)\n\n**Repair:**\nThe learning rate should be reduced to a reasonable value for Adam. A good default would be 0.001.",
